    "content": "<h4>Altar of Weeping</h4>\n<p><em>5th-Level Conjuration</em></p>\n<p><strong>Casting Time:</strong> :: 10 Minutes (Incantation)<br><strong>Range:</strong>        :: 10 feet<br><strong>Components:</strong>   :: V,S<br><strong>Duration:</strong>     :: 24 Hours</p>\n<p>You create an Altar of Weeping at a location within Range. The Altar of Weeping is an object with AC 10 and 50 Hit Points. It has Resistance to Physical Damage, and is Immune to Psychic, Poison, and Necrotic Damage. A minute after creating the Altar, it becomes active.<br>At the end of each of your Turns while the Altar of Weeping is active, the closest Creature within 100 feet of the Altar must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be overwhelmed by the great sorrow of the Altar until the end of their next Turn. While they are overwhelmed, their Speed is halved, they cannot take Reactions, and during their Turn they must choose between taking an Action or a Bonus Action. However, while overwhelmed, a Creature can release a sorrowful wail as an Action, damaging the psyche of all who hear it. All other Creatures within a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on that Creature must make a Wisdom Saving Throw, taking 4d8 Psychic Damage on a failed Save, or half as much on a successful Save.<br><strong>At Higher Levels:</strong> For each Level above 5 it is cast at, the Altar targets 1 additional Creature at the end of your Turn. It cannot target the same Creature twice on a Turn.</p>",
    "rawSource": "#### Altar of Weeping\n*5th-Level Conjuration*\n\n**Casting Time:** :: 10 Minutes (Incantation)\n**Range:**        :: 10 feet\n**Components:**   :: V,S\n**Duration:**     :: 24 Hours\n\nYou create an Altar of Weeping at a location within Range. The Altar of Weeping is an object with AC 10 and 50 Hit Points. It has Resistance to Physical Damage, and is Immune to Psychic, Poison, and Necrotic Damage. A minute after creating the Altar, it becomes active.\n:\nAt the end of each of your Turns while the Altar of Weeping is active, the closest Creature within 100 feet of the Altar must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be overwhelmed by the great sorrow of the Altar until the end of their next Turn. While they are overwhelmed, their Speed is halved, they cannot take Reactions, and during their Turn they must choose between taking an Action or a Bonus Action. However, while overwhelmed, a Creature can release a sorrowful wail as an Action, damaging the psyche of all who hear it. All other Creatures within a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on that Creature must make a Wisdom Saving Throw, taking 4d8 Psychic Damage on a failed Save, or half as much on a successful Save.\n:\n**At Higher Levels:** For each Level above 5 it is cast at, the Altar targets 1 additional Creature at the end of your Turn. It cannot target the same Creature twice on a Turn.\n\n\\column"
