    "castingMetadata": {
      "casting": "1 Minute",
      "range": "Self",
      "components": "V, S",
      "duration": "Concentration, up to 10 Minutes."
    },
    "content": "<h4>Avatar of Wind</h4>\n<p><em>9th-Level Evocation</em></p>\n<p><strong>Casting Time:</strong> :: 1 Minute<br><strong>Range:</strong>        :: Self<br><strong>Components:</strong>   :: V, S<br><strong>Duration:</strong>     :: Concentration, up to 10 Minutes.</p>\n<p>For a brief time, you achieve complete mastery of the four winds. Until the Art ends, gale-force winds whip around you like armour. For the duration of the Art:</p>\n<p>• You gain a Fly Speed of 100ft. If you are still flying when the Art ends, you descend gracefully to the ground at a pace of 100 feet per Turn; you do not take falling Damage.</p>\n<p>• The area within a 30-foot-radius of you is considered to be Difficult Terrain for all other Creatures, except those designated by you when you cast this Art. You may change any number of designated Creatures during your Turn.</p>\n<p>• Non-Magical Ranged Attacks against you automatically miss.</p>\n<p>• When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half Damage, you instead take no Damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and only half Damage if you fail.</p>\n<p>• As a Bonus Action during your Turn, choose a point within 100 feet that you can see. All Creatures in a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on that point must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 5d6 Bludgeoning Damage, and you may then choose whether Creatures that failed the Save are pulled 15 feet towards the centre of the area, or pushed 15 feet away from the centre of the area. Creatures that succeed on the Saving Throw take half as much Damage, and suffer no other effects.</p>",
    "rawSource": "#### Avatar of Wind\n*9th-Level Evocation*\n\n**Casting Time:** :: 1 Minute\n**Range:**        :: Self\n**Components:**   :: V, S\n**Duration:**     :: Concentration, up to 10 Minutes.\n\nFor a brief time, you achieve complete mastery of the four winds. Until the Art ends, gale-force winds whip around you like armour. For the duration of the Art:\n- You gain a Fly Speed of 100ft. If you are still flying when the Art ends, you descend gracefully to the ground at a pace of 100 feet per Turn; you do not take falling Damage. \n- The area within a 30-foot-radius of you is considered to be Difficult Terrain for all other Creatures, except those designated by you when you cast this Art. You may change any number of designated Creatures during your Turn. \n- Non-Magical Ranged Attacks against you automatically miss.\n- When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half Damage, you instead take no Damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and only half Damage if you fail.\n- As a Bonus Action during your Turn, choose a point within 100 feet that you can see. All Creatures in a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on that point must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 5d6 Bludgeoning Damage, and you may then choose whether Creatures that failed the Save are pulled 15 feet towards the centre of the area, or pushed 15 feet away from the centre of the area. Creatures that succeed on the Saving Throw take half as much Damage, and suffer no other effects."
