    "castingMetadata": {
      "casting": "Action",
      "range": "250 feet",
      "components": "V,S",
      "duration": "Concentration, up to 1 minute"
    },
    "content": "<h4>Event Horizon</h4>\n<p><em>9th-Level Evocation</em></p>\n<p><strong>Casting Time:</strong> :: Action<br><strong>Range:</strong>        :: 250 feet<br><strong>Components:</strong>   :: V,S<br><strong>Duration:</strong>     :: Concentration, up to 1 minute</p>\n<p>You create an incredibly dense point of gravity in a 50-foot-radius sphere centred on a point you can see within range. The area within this sphere is considered to be Difficult Terrain; this applies even through solid objects.<br>At the start of each of your Turns, every Creature within the sphere must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 3d10 Force Damage and are pulled 20 feet towards the centre of the area. On a successful Save, they take half as much Damage, and are not pulled. Unsecured Objects are pulled 20 feet towards the centre automatically.<br>This pull is capable of pulling Creatures and Objects into the air unless they are secured to the ground in some way, such as by grabbing hold of objects that are secured. Creatures and Objects pulled into the air are suspended there until they return to the ground, escape the area, or the spell ends; in which case they fall directly downwards. A Creature that does not have a Fly or Hover Speed can only move by pushing or pulling against objects, including objects which are suspended.<br>If a Creature is pulled into the centre of the sphere, they take 8d10 Force Damage. A Creature that is reduced to 0 Hit Points by this Damage is instantly killed, crushed into an unrecognisable mass.<br>When you cast this Art, you may designate a number of Creatures you can see equal to your Spellcasting Ability Modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. Those Creatures automatically succeed on the Saving Throw.<br>[Credit](https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells/2628064-gravity-well)</p>",
    "rawSource": "#### Event Horizon\n*9th-Level Evocation*\n\n**Casting Time:** :: Action\n**Range:**        :: 250 feet\n**Components:**   :: V,S\n**Duration:**     :: Concentration, up to 1 minute\n\nYou create an incredibly dense point of gravity in a 50-foot-radius sphere centred on a point you can see within range. The area within this sphere is considered to be Difficult Terrain; this applies even through solid objects.\n:\nAt the start of each of your Turns, every Creature within the sphere must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 3d10 Force Damage and are pulled 20 feet towards the centre of the area. On a successful Save, they take half as much Damage, and are not pulled. Unsecured Objects are pulled 20 feet towards the centre automatically. \n:\nThis pull is capable of pulling Creatures and Objects into the air unless they are secured to the ground in some way, such as by grabbing hold of objects that are secured. Creatures and Objects pulled into the air are suspended there until they return to the ground, escape the area, or the spell ends; in which case they fall directly downwards. A Creature that does not have a Fly or Hover Speed can only move by pushing or pulling against objects, including objects which are suspended.  \n:\nIf a Creature is pulled into the centre of the sphere, they take 8d10 Force Damage. A Creature that is reduced to 0 Hit Points by this Damage is instantly killed, crushed into an unrecognisable mass. \n:\nWhen you cast this Art, you may designate a number of Creatures you can see equal to your Spellcasting Ability Modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. Those Creatures automatically succeed on the Saving Throw.\n:\n[Credit](https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells/2628064-gravity-well)\n\n}}\n\n{{imageMaskEdge1,--offset:-2%,--rotation:-5\n<img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/d/da/IS-Those_Who_Open_The_Door.png?f348fe' \n  style='position:absolute;top:360px;right:-400px;width:1500px' />\n}}\n\n\n\\page\n{{pageNumber,auto}}"
