    "content": "<h4>Mountainfall</h4>\n<p><em>9th-Level Conjuration</em></p>\n<p><strong>Casting Time:</strong> :: Action<br><strong>Range:</strong>        :: 500 feet<br><strong>Components:</strong>   :: V, S<br><strong>Duration:</strong>     :: Instant</p>\n<p>Raising up earth and stone from a massive area, you crash it down in a 50-foot-radius sphere centred on a grounded point you can see within range. Every Creature within the area must make a Dexterity Saving Throw; they take 8d6 Bludgeoning Damage on a failed Save, or half as much on a successful Save.<br>Creatures who took Damage from the initial cast of the Art are buried under rock and rubble. They must make a Strength Saving Throw at the beginning of their Turn until they have left the area to resist being crushed. On a failed Save, they take 4d6 Bludgeoning Damage, or half as much on a successful Save.</p>",
