    "content": "<h4>Tug the Heartstrings</h4>\n<p><em>7th-Level Necromancy (Haemomancy)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Casting Time:</strong> :: Action<br><strong>Range:</strong>        :: 50 feet<br><strong>Components:</strong>   :: V,S<br><strong>Duration:</strong>     :: Concentration, up to 10 Minutes.</p>\n<p>By controlling the movement of blood in a Creature you can see, you can practically control their movements.<br>Choose a Creature you can see within range; that Creature must make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed Save, you control their actions during their Turn; you cannot cause them to cast Arts, they have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls, and if you would attempt any action that would be immediately harmful to them (such as leaping from a high location), they may immediately attempt the Saving Throw again, ending the effect on a success. On a successful Saving Throw, they are instead Dazed until the end of their next Turn.<br>A Creature being controlled by you may reattempt the Saving Throw at the end of their Turn, ending the effect on a success.<br><strong>Blood Amber:</strong> If there is a Blood Amber within 50 feet of you when a Creature makes a Saving Throw against this Art cast by you, you can consume that Blood Amber to give them Disadvantage on that Saving Throw.</p>",
    "rawSource": "#### Tug the Heartstrings\n*7th-Level Necromancy (Haemomancy)*\n\n**Casting Time:** :: Action \n**Range:**        :: 50 feet\n**Components:**   :: V,S\n**Duration:**     :: Concentration, up to 10 Minutes.\n\nBy controlling the movement of blood in a Creature you can see, you can practically control their movements. \n:\nChoose a Creature you can see within range; that Creature must make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed Save, you control their actions during their Turn; you cannot cause them to cast Arts, they have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls, and if you would attempt any action that would be immediately harmful to them (such as leaping from a high location), they may immediately attempt the Saving Throw again, ending the effect on a success. On a successful Saving Throw, they are instead Dazed until the end of their next Turn. \n:\nA Creature being controlled by you may reattempt the Saving Throw at the end of their Turn, ending the effect on a success.\n:\n**Blood Amber:** If there is a Blood Amber within 50 feet of you when a Creature makes a Saving Throw against this Art cast by you, you can consume that Blood Amber to give them Disadvantage on that Saving Throw.\n\n\\page\n{{pageNumber,auto}}"
