    "content": "<h4>Ultimate Necrostorm</h4>\n<p><em>9th-level Necromancy</em></p>\n<p><strong>Casting Time:</strong> :: Action<br><strong>Range:</strong>        :: 500 feet<br><strong>Components:</strong>   :: V,S<br><strong>Duration:</strong>     :: Instant</p>\n<p>Choose a point you can see within range; you begin channelling your Arts as a swirling hurricane of foul mist builds around the chosen point. As an Action on your following Turn, all Creatures within a 50-foot-radius sphere centred on that point must make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 7d10 Necrotic Damage and are Poisoned. On a successful Save, they take half as much Damage only.<br>A Creature Poisoned in this way can reattempt the Saving Throw at the end of each of their Turns, ending the Condition on a success.</p>",
